Ontology-Practice
Copyright 2026 BKN contributors

Ontology-Practice is inspired by the BKN (Business Knowledge Network) ontology
theory of AISHU (爱数). It is an independent engineering practice for product
operations (运维): the goal is to make operations knowledge runnable, machine-
checkable and evolvable, not to cover general-purpose BKN methodology.

It also references the methodology of OpenBKN Engineering (Apache-2.0) as an
external comparison only; no source file from that project is copied here.
